      "version": "1.0.1",
      "wrapperType": "software",
      "currency": "USD",
      "description": "Scan locally for nearby smart glasses Bluetooth signals and get a clear alert when a likely device is close.\n\nThe app uses your device to show active signals from smart glasses, Meta Glasses, Meta Ray Bans, Snap Spectacles, Amazon Echo Frames, and RayNeo. It will also show you repeat sightings, confidence, and rough proximity from the devices. \n\nFeatures:\n- Live signal field: likely glasses appear as blips with rough proximity and confidence\n- Local alerts the moment a likely device starts broadcasting — even with the app closed\n- Sightings history: repeat encounters, confidence, distance, and why each signal was flagged\n- Register your own glasses so they never trigger alerts, and see when they were last heard\n- Snooze alerts for an hour or the evening, right from the notification\n- Home-screen and Lock Screen widgets with the latest status and a pause button\n- Control Center toggle to pause or resume scanning, even assignable to the Action Button\n- No account, no ads, completely local and private\n\nPrivacy stays local. The app does not identify people, record audio or video, track location, or upload signal history. Detection is best-effort and depends on what nearby devices advertise over Bluetooth: smart glasses mostly broadcast at power-on, pairing, and case-open, so coverage is opportunistic.",
